from (values
('127.164.d.4',3,'A student animation team imports sketches, edits sound, and exports video using computer programs. This shows that they:','["Apply technology applications to their work", "Use only paper", "Avoid all software", "Skip production"]'::jsonb,0,'Technology applications in animation.','original'),
('127.164.d.4',4,'Which pairing shows correct use of an application for its job?','["Using a spreadsheet to sculpt a character", "Using a video editor to trim and join clips", "Using a browser to record dialogue", "Using a calculator to paint a background"]'::jsonb,1,'Match the tool to the task.','original'),
('127.164.d.5',3,'Before opening an unknown email attachment sent to a studio computer, a student should:','["Forward it to everyone", "Turn off the antivirus", "Check with the teacher or IT first", "Open it at once"]'::jsonb,2,'Cyber safety procedure.','original'),
('127.164.d.5',4,'Using a different strong password for each animation account mainly protects against:','["Large file sizes", "Slow renders", "Low frame rates", "One breach exposing every account"]'::jsonb,3,'Password safety.','original'),
('127.164.d.8',3,'A student saves a rig as a template so it can be reused on new characters. This is an advanced technique for:','["Working more efficiently", "Wasting time", "Lowering quality", "Erasing layers"]'::jsonb,0,'Technical efficiency.','original'),
('127.164.d.8',4,'Scripting a repeated task, such as renaming 200 frames, helps an animator by:','["Lowering resolution", "Saving hours of manual work", "Creating more frames", "Deleting the project"]'::jsonb,1,'Advanced efficiency.','original'),
('127.164.d.1.A',3,'When a student proofreads a shot list for spelling and clear sentences, which subject skill are they using?','["Welding", "Gardening", "English language arts", "Cooking"]'::jsonb,2,'ELA applied in animation.','original'),
('127.164.d.1.A',4,'Writing a short artist statement for an animated project requires:','["Only pictures", "Only numbers", "Random notes", "Clear writing and correct grammar"]'::jsonb,3,'Writing skills.','original'),
('127.164.d.1.B',3,'An animated clip runs 8 seconds at 12 drawings per second. How many drawings are needed?','["96", "20", "108", "64"]'::jsonb,0,'8 x 12 = 96.','original'),
('127.164.d.1.B',4,'A background is 4800 pixels wide and the screen shows 1200 pixels at a time. How many screens wide is the background?','["40", "4", "6", "3"]'::jsonb,1,'4800 / 1200 = 4.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.A',3,'A student explains a storyboard to second graders using simple words and gestures. This is adapting language to the:','["Hard drive", "Frame rate", "Audience", "Render farm"]'::jsonb,2,'Adapt language.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.A',4,'Describing a character''s motivation to a teacher versus to a friend requires changing the:','["Software version", "Spelling of names", "Frame size", "Tone and vocabulary for each listener"]'::jsonb,3,'Audience and situation.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.B',3,'Putting storyboard panels in numbered order before a pitch is a way to:','["Organize information", "Hide the story", "Lower the volume", "Shorten the film"]'::jsonb,0,'Organize information.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.B',4,'A pitch that goes problem, characters, solution is organized by:','["Alphabet", "Logical sequence", "Random order", "Color"]'::jsonb,1,'Organization.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.C',3,'A team member explains what a critique chart means in plain language. That is:','["Rendering a scene", "Capturing audio", "Interpreting and communicating information", "Rigging a model"]'::jsonb,2,'Interpret information.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.C',4,'A graph shows viewers dropping off at the 20-second mark of a short. The team should:','["Delete the whole film", "Ignore the graph", "Add credits", "Review what happens at that point"]'::jsonb,3,'Interpret data.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.D',3,'A class screening where students present finished shorts with slides is a:','["Formal presentation", "Sound check", "Casual chat", "Backup"]'::jsonb,0,'Formal presentation.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.D',4,'Giving a quick two-minute progress update at your desk to a partner is a(n):','["Awards show", "Informal presentation", "Press release", "Formal keynote"]'::jsonb,1,'Informal presentation.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.E',3,'During critique, active listening includes:','["Checking messages", "Interrupting", "Eye contact and taking notes", "Talking over others"]'::jsonb,2,'Active listening.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.E',4,'After a peer gives feedback, the best way to show you listened is to:','["Walk away", "Argue every point", "Change the subject", "Restate the main points in your own words"]'::jsonb,3,'Confirming understanding.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.F',3,'A classmate who speaks another language joins your animation team. A respectful action is to:','["Use clear words and visuals so they can contribute", "Exclude them", "Talk faster", "Ignore their ideas"]'::jsonb,0,'Diverse individuals.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.F',4,'Hearing ideas from students of different backgrounds can improve an animation by:','["Shrinking the screen", "Adding more varied story and design choices", "Cutting the soundtrack", "Slowing the render"]'::jsonb,1,'Value of diversity.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.G',3,'Public relations skills in a student studio include:','["Staying silent", "Hiding the film", "Presenting the team''s work politely to visitors", "Arguing with guests"]'::jsonb,2,'PR skills.','original'),
('127.164.d.2.G',4,'When a visitor asks a tough question about your short, a good PR response is to:','["Leave", "Get defensive", "Ignore them", "Answer calmly and thank them for asking"]'::jsonb,3,'Professional communication.','original'),
('127.164.d.3.A',3,'Weighing the pros and cons of two color palettes before choosing one is:','["Critical thinking", "Copying", "Procrastinating", "Guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Critical thinking.','original'),
('127.164.d.3.A',4,'A group tests two camera moves and picks the one viewers understood better. This is decision making based on:','["Speed only", "Evidence", "Volume", "Luck"]'::jsonb,1,'Group critical thinking.','original'),
('127.164.d.3.B',3,'Two teammates want different endings. A helpful interpersonal skill is:','["Quitting", "Insulting", "Listening and finding a compromise", "Refusing to talk"]'::jsonb,2,'Interpersonal skills.','original'),
('127.164.d.3.B',4,'Using "I" statements such as "I feel the scene drags" helps a group because it:','["Ends discussion", "Blames people", "Hides the problem", "Keeps feedback respectful and focused"]'::jsonb,3,'Group communication.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.A',3,'A team leader who sets a goal, lists steps, and checks progress is:','["Employing leadership skills", "Working alone", "Delaying", "Avoiding work"]'::jsonb,0,'Leadership.','original'),
