('127.164.d.6.C',4,'Constructive feedback on a rough animation should be:','["Vague and harsh", "Specific and focused on improving the work", "Personal", "Delayed for weeks"]'::jsonb,1,'Constructive feedback.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.D',3,'Before a team meeting, a student prepares by writing:','["A joke book", "A grocery list", "Goals and an agenda", "A new password"]'::jsonb,2,'Meeting preparation.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.D',4,'A meeting objective such as "decide the title font today" is useful because it is:','["Hidden", "Vague", "Endless", "Specific and measurable"]'::jsonb,3,'Objectives.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.E',3,'A good meeting participant:','["Stays on topic and takes turns", "Interrupts often", "Browses games", "Leaves early"]'::jsonb,0,'Meeting conduct.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.E',4,'The best way to end a meeting is to:','["Add new topics", "Review decisions and assign tasks", "Forget notes", "End abruptly"]'::jsonb,1,'Meeting outcomes.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.F',3,'A student who teaches a younger classmate how to use a drawing tablet is:','["Quitting", "Copying", "Mentoring", "Competing"]'::jsonb,2,'Mentoring.','original'),
('127.164.d.6.F',4,'Good mentors inspire others by being:','["Secretive", "Critical of everything", "Impatient", "Patient and encouraging"]'::jsonb,3,'Mentoring.','original'),
('127.164.d.7.A',3,'Giving credit to every classmate who helped make a short is:','["Ethical conduct", "Optional", "Unfair", "A mistake"]'::jsonb,0,'Ethical conduct.','original'),
('127.164.d.7.A',4,'Claiming a partner''s character design as your own is:','["Teamwork", "Dishonest", "Allowed", "Efficient"]'::jsonb,1,'Ethics.','original'),
('127.164.d.7.B',4,'Using a popular song in a school film shared online without permission may:','["Be free of rules", "Be encouraged", "Break copyright law", "Be required"]'::jsonb,2,'Copyright application.','original'),
